    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="32ea2643-bf33-5ec1-8d1a-d4d20d410ad0" activityNameId="4823f65e-06ca-5d38-9e5c-238ce0c7701b" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, frit for CRT tube production, to residual material landfill</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, frit for CRT tube production, to residual material landfill
Inventoried waste contains 100% Frit; . waste composition (wet, in ppm): H2O n.a.; O 152000; H n.a.; C n.a.; S n.a.; N n.a.; P n.a.; B 28000; Cl n.a.; Br n.a.; F n.a.; I n.a.; Ag n.a.; As n.a.; Ba 18000; Cd n.a.; Co n.a.; Cr n.a.; Cu n.a.; Hg n.a.; Mn n.a.; Mo n.a.; Ni n.a.; Pb 696000; Sb n.a.; Se n.a.; Sn n.a.; V n.a.; Zn 96000; Be n.a.; Sc n.a.; Sr n.a.; Ti n.a.; Tl n.a.; W n.a.; Si 10000; Fe n.a.; Ca n.a.; Al n.a.; K n.a.; Mg n.a.; Na n.a.; Share of carbon in waste that is biogenic 60.4%. Additional solidification with 0.4 kg of cement.;; UUID: da26f8ab-3b0a-4765-8d6a-d0ab4d173bb1
Waste-specific short-term emissions to water from leachate. Long-term emissions from landfill to ground water. Expenditures for solidificalion with cement (user-specified option)
Location: Technology encountered in Switzerland in 2000. Landfill includes base seal and leachate collection system.
Technology: Swiss residual material landfill for polluted, inorganic waste. With base seal and leachate collection system. Recultivation after closure. 
Time period: Waste composition as given in literature reference, theoretical data or other source. Transfer coefficients from prospective model.
Production volume: na
Sampling: Landfill model based on observed leachate concentrations in literature. Extrapolated to 60'000 years heeding chemical characteristics. Initial waste composition from various literature sources. 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: uncertainty of waste input composition data derived from generic formula GSD(c) = N*ln(c)+1. Minimal long-term emissions are the emissions until the carbonate buffer in the landfill is used up. Mean long-term emissions are the emissions until the next glacial period occurs (in 60'000a) and the landfill is eroded. Maximal long-term emissions are the complete emissions of all landfilled material (except Cr).
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_da26f8ab-3b0a-4765-8d6a-d0ab4d173bb1.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
